# ==============================================================================
# FISHERY-AI INGESTION GATEWAY & BRAIN GOVERNANCE (/fishery-ai/)
# ==============================================================================
# Scope: Node.js Edge AI Service, Telegram Telegraf/Bot Engine, Ollama / Gemini

## 1. FILE HEADER PATH LOGGING LAW
- Every modified or created file MUST start with the absolute path comment on line 1:
  - JavaScript: `// File: fishery-ai/services/ai.service.js`
  - Docker/Modelfile: `# File: fishery-ai/Modelfile`

## 2. CRITICAL ALGORITHM & INFERENCE IMMUNITY
- PROTECTED CORE: Do not refactor, truncate, or restructure the core processing units in:
  - `services/ai.service.js` (Dual Cloud-to-Edge AI fallback pipeline)
  - `services/isdalog.api.js` (Ecosystem HTTP bridge)
  - `services/weather.service.js` (Open-Meteo port wind speed & safety threshold evaluator)
  - `Modelfile` (VRAM optimization parameters)
- Dual-Tier Inference Rules:
  - Cloud tier (`gemini-2.5-flash`) MUST maintain timeout thresholds (`7000ms`).
  - Edge fallback tier (`llama3.2-vision:latest`) MUST use explicit `http.Agent` socket pooling with `keepAlive: false` and `num_ctx 512` constraints to prevent GPU memory saturation.
  - Failover state must always resolve to `{ species: "Unknown Fish", engine: "failed" }` instead of throwing unhandled process crashes.

## 3. STATE MACHINE & SESSION INTEGRITY
- Telegram conversation state sequence in `index.js` is invariant:
  `AWAITING_SPECIES` -> `AWAITING_WEIGHT` -> `AWAITING_PRICE` -> `AWAITING_PORT_CHOICE` -> `AWAITING_CONFIRMATION`
- Input Sanitization Law: All text inputs for weight and price MUST pass through `sanitizeNumericInput()` before updating session objects to prevent NaN propagation to the core API.
- Process Resilience: Top-level listeners for `unhandledRejection`, `uncaughtException`, and `polling_error` must remain intact at all times.

## 4. STRICT ZERO PLACEHOLDERS & COMPLETE CODE
- Full source output only. Never emit incomplete callback trees, missing action cases in `bot.on('callback_query')`, or partial regex parsers.
- CommonJS standard: Enforce `require()` / `module.exports` syntax in accordance with `package.json` (`"type": "commonjs"`).